{"id":"priest","name":"Priest","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:priest"],"groups":["Before Moses","Duties Of","Examine lepers","Carry the ark of the covenant","Benefits Of","(The function he served was superior to that of other priests)","For qualifications, consecration, etc","Benefits of","Miscellaneous Facts Concerning","Instances of"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Priest","text":"The Heb. kohen, Gr. hierus, Lat. sacerdos, always denote one who offers sacrifices. At first every man was his own priest, and presented his own sacrifices before God. Afterwards that office devolved on the head of the family, as in the cases of Noah (Gen. 8:20), Abraham (12:7; 13:4), Isaac (26:25), Jacob (31:54), and Job (Job 1:5). The name first occurs as applied to Melchizedek (Gen. 14:18). Under the Levitical arrangements the office of the priesthood was limited to the tribe of Levi, and to only one family of that tribe, the family of Aaron. Certain laws respecting the qualifications of priests are given in Lev. 21:16-23. There are ordinances also regarding the priests’ dress (Ex. 28:40-43) and the manner of their consecration to the office (29:1-37). Their duties were manifold (Ex. 27:20, 21; 29:38-44; Lev. 6:12; 10:11; 24:8; Num. 10:1-10; Deut. 17:8-13; 33:10; Mal. 2:7). They …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H175","lemma":"אַהֲרוֹן","xlit":"ʼAhărôwn","gloss":"Aharon, the brother of Moses","kjv":"Aaron","count":106,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H3881","lemma":"לֵוִיִּי","xlit":"Lêvîyîy","gloss":"a Levite or descendant of Levi","kjv":"Leviite","count":86,"share":0.1},{"strong":"H6944","lemma":"קֹדֶשׁ","xlit":"qôdesh","gloss":"a sacred place or thing","kjv":"consecrated, dedicated, hallowed, holiness","count":86,"share":0.1},{"strong":"G749","lemma":"ἀρχιερεύς","xlit":"archiereús","gloss":"the high-priest","kjv":"chief  priest, chief of the priests","count":55,"share":0.06},{"strong":"H4196","lemma":"מִזְבֵּחַ","xlit":"mizbêach","gloss":"an altar","kjv":"altar","